Quasar-authored. Issue #428 — one GstCaps leaked per caps-compatibility check.

gst_inter_pipe_sink_are_caps_compatible() computes
`renegotiated_caps = gst_caps_intersect (listener_caps, sinkcaps)` and returns on
BOTH paths without unreffing it. gst_caps_intersect() is (transfer full), so every
call leaks exactly one GstCaps.

Reached from gst_inter_pipe_sink_add_listener() only when the sink has already
negotiated caps, other listeners are attached, and the listener's caps differ from
the sink's — rare in Quasar's single-format topology, which is why it is low
priority — but unbounded where it does fire, and invisible to a
`leaks(filters=GstObject)` census (a GstCaps is a GstMiniObject, and after teardown
no live GstObject holds it), exactly like the #418 leak.

Restructured so the function has one exit: the compatible/incompatible decision and
its log line both happen before the unref, and the unref happens on the way out.

Applies to the ${GST_INTERPIPE_REF} checkout alongside
interpipesink-add-listener-caps-leak.patch; the two touch different functions
(~line 345 vs ~line 980) and are order-independent. Verified in the dev container:
meson build clean, full suite 15/15 green (gst_test_caps_renegotiation and
gst_test_invalid_caps exercise this path).

diff --git a/gst/interpipe/gstinterpipesink.c b/gst/interpipe/gstinterpipesink.c
index 4e0acfc..c2500b1 100644
--- a/gst/interpipe/gstinterpipesink.c
+++ b/gst/interpipe/gstinterpipesink.c
@@ -346,18 +346,24 @@ gst_inter_pipe_sink_are_caps_compatible (GstInterPipeSink * sink,
     GstCaps * listener_caps, GstCaps * sinkcaps)
 {
   GstCaps *renegotiated_caps = NULL;
+  gboolean compatible;
 
+  /* gst_caps_intersect() is (transfer full): the result is ours to release on
+   * BOTH exit paths. It used to be released on neither, leaking one GstCaps per
+   * call whenever the listener and the sink negotiated different caps. */
   renegotiated_caps = gst_caps_intersect (listener_caps, sinkcaps);
 
-  if (gst_caps_is_empty (renegotiated_caps)) {
+  compatible = !gst_caps_is_empty (renegotiated_caps);
+  if (compatible) {
+    GST_INFO_OBJECT (sink, "Renegotiated caps: %" GST_PTR_FORMAT,
+        renegotiated_caps);
+  } else {
     GST_ERROR_OBJECT (sink, "No caps intersection between listener and sink");
-    return FALSE;
   }
 
-  GST_INFO_OBJECT (sink, "Renegotiated caps: %" GST_PTR_FORMAT,
-      renegotiated_caps);
+  gst_caps_unref (renegotiated_caps);
 
-  return TRUE;
+  return compatible;
 }
 
 static GstCaps *

